{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>These are the heads, etc.</b> The reason Scripture brought up the number of the children of Israel up to Moses is in accordance with what I explained nearby, that He appointed them as rulers over Israel — Scripture traces their lineage to show that over Israel one appoints only those whose lineage traces back to Jacob. Therefore Scripture did not trace their lineage beforehand, but only after the statement of Moses, ״הֵן בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל,״ and the response of HaShem to him, וַיְצַוֵּם, whereby He appointed them as rulers — and this is correct."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:10.787360341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}